## Project State Summary

**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment that regenerates Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specifications, verified via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.

**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human operator writes PRDs and use cases; the orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`; differential testing via `pkg/testutils` verifies output parity against Homebrew GNU binaries.

**Current state:** 17 commands implemented across generations 1-17 (tee, head, seq, echo, tac, nl, fold, expand, unexpand, cut, paste, uniq, comm, md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum). All releases through rel05.4 are marked `implemented`. Shared packages (pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format) exist at generation-merged tags.

**Current release:** rel99.2 — the only remaining release with `spec_complete` status. Contains one use case: `rel99.2-uc001-ts` (the `ts` moreutils timestamp utility). Code status: not started on the current branch despite earlier generation tags existing.

## Priority Analysis

rel99.2 is the only release in scope. It contains a single use case (`ts`). Per P2, implementation and tests should be split. With the 1-task constraint, the implementation task takes priority (P8: implementation before tests). The `ts` utility is a moreutils tool — the stitch agent needs explicit guidance that the reference binary may not be available and must use `t.Skip` via `exec.LookPath` (learned from sponge container issue in project memory).

```yaml
- index: 0
  title: "cmd/ts: implement ts utility (prd-ts core requirements)"
  dependency: -1
  description: |
    deliverable_type: code

    required_reading:
      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-ts.yaml (all requirements for ts)
      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel99.2-uc001-ts.yaml (end-to-end execution path)
      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-99.2.yaml (test cases and expected behavior)
      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern, SIGPIPE handling)
      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)
      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests signature)
      - cmd/tac/main.go (reference for stdin-reading utility structure and differential test setup)

    files:
      - path: cmd/ts/main.go
        action: create
        note: ts utility implementation -- reads stdin, prepends timestamps to each line
      - path: cmd/ts/ts_test.go
        action: create
        note: differential tests against reference ts binary from moreutils

    requirements:
      - id: R1
        text: |
          Implement the ts command that reads lines from stdin and prepends a
          timestamp to each line. The default format is the strftime-style format
          from the PRD (read prd004-ts.yaml for the exact default). Accept an
          optional format string as a positional argument. Implement all flags
          specified in prd004-ts.yaml (typically -s for relative time since start,
          -i for incremental time between lines, -m for monotonic clock). Follow
          the PRD requirements exactly for flag behavior and format string handling.
      - id: R2
        text: |
          Handle stream behavior correctly: read from stdin line by line, flush
          output after each line (line-buffered output). Exit 0 on normal
          completion or when stdin reaches EOF. Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()
          at the start of main to match GNU behavior when piped to a consumer that
          closes its stdin early.
      - id: R3
        text: |
          Support the %.S or sub-second precision format specifier if documented in
          the PRD. Replace %.S (or the PRD-specified sub-second token) with the
          fractional seconds before passing the format to Go's time formatting. Map
          strftime format specifiers to Go time layout equivalents as specified in
          the PRD.
      - id: R4
        text: |
          Write differential tests in ts_test.go using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests.
          Build the Go binary with testutils.BuildBinary. Look up the reference
          binary with exec.LookPath("ts") -- if not found, call t.Skip (the
          reference binary is from moreutils which may not be installed). Define
          test cases as []testutils.DiffTest covering: default format, custom format
          string, -s flag, -i flag, and flag combinations from the test suite spec.
          Use testutils.TimestampNormalizer or a custom NormalizeFunc to handle
          timestamp value differences between the two binaries (timestamps will
          differ by milliseconds).

    design_decisions:
      - id: D1
        text: |
          Do NOT install any packages in the build or test environment. The
          reference binary (ts from moreutils) may not be available. Use
          exec.LookPath("ts") and t.Skip gracefully if not found.
      - id: D2
        text: |
          Use Go's time package for formatting. Build a strftime-to-Go format
          mapping function to convert strftime directives (%Y, %m, %d, %H, %M,
          %S, etc.) to Go layout equivalents. Handle %.S sub-second precision
          separately since Go's time.Format does not have a strftime equivalent.
      - id: D3
        text: |
          Follow the same cmd/ package structure as other utilities in this
          project. main.go contains all implementation code. ts_test.go contains
          only differential tests. Use flag package for argument parsing.
      - id: D4
        text: |
          For differential tests, timestamps between the Go and reference binary
          will differ. Use a NormalizeFunc that replaces timestamp portions of
          output with a fixed string before comparison, or use a regex-based
          normalizer that validates format structure without exact value matching.

    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: AC1
        text: cmd/ts/main.go compiles without errors via "go build ./cmd/ts/"
      - id: AC2
        text: "Running echo 'hello' | go run ./cmd/ts/ produces output with a timestamp prefix followed by 'hello'"
      - id: AC3
        text: All flags documented in prd004-ts.yaml are implemented and accepted by the argument parser
      - id: AC4
        text: cmd/ts/ts_test.go exists with differential tests using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests
      - id: AC5
        text: "Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when the reference ts binary is not in PATH"
      - id: AC6
        text: "go test ./cmd/ts/ passes (either running differential tests or skipping if reference binary absent)"
      - id: AC7
        text: pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at the start of main()
```